{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Single colour authority for every map and legend of the visual board and the reports (docs/BOARD_COLORS_KO.md). Colour = peril family, darkness = magnitude. Class breaks are fixed per quantity and never derived from the data on screen, so a map never re-scales between return periods, years, scenarios or regions.",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "updated": "2026-11-11",
    "ramp_sources": "ColorBrewer 2.0 (Brewer, Harrower 2003; Blues, Reds, RdPu, BuGn, PiYG, PRGn purple arm, BrBG brown arm), first steps of dryness and ground darkened so the lightest class stays apart from the shared zero colour",
    "checks": "tests/test_board_palettes.py: lightness strictly falls along every ramp (OKLab L), families differ by >= 10 OKLab dE x100 at ramp steps 2-4, every class colour is a step of its family ramp in ramp order, the lightest class differs from zero by >= 8, breaks strictly increase, every peril in perils.json has a family.",
    "class_rule": "value null/NaN -> shared.null; value == 0 and zero_means_none -> shared.zero; value <= breaks[0] -> class 0; breaks[i-1] < value <= breaks[i] -> class i; value > breaks[-1] -> last class. Class i uses family ramp[steps[i]]. spei_stage: first stage (driest first) with value <= leq, else shared.zero. change: same break rule on the ratio with change.colors."
  },
